  "finalAnswer": "For educational purposes, typical warning signs of anaphylaxis that affect the **breathing system** and the **circulatory system** include:\n\n**Breathing signs:**\n*   Trouble breathing or shortness of breath\n*   Sensation of throat tightness, swelling of the throat or tongue\n*   Wheezing or stridor (a high-pitched noise when breathing)\n\n**Circulation signs:**\n*   Weak pulse or rapid pulse (fast heartbeat)\n*   Lightheadedness, dizziness, or feeling faint\n*   Loss of consciousness\n\n**Important:** This information is for general education only and does not diagnose a condition. Anaphylaxis is a serious medical emergency requiring immediate professional help. General medical descriptions can vary among individuals, and additional symptoms not listed here may also occur.",
